This repository holds two kinds of material, and they are not under the same
terms. Saying so is not a formality: the Prime World sources are published under
an agreement whose section 4 requires that a licensee's modifications be
distributed freely, at no cost, and without additional commercial restrictions.
A repository with no licence file at all is, by default, all rights reserved -
which is exactly such a restriction. Hence this file.


1. Our own work: MIT
--------------------

Everything under cmake/, stubs/ and tools/, and the build scaffolding of the
workflows in .github/workflows/, is ours and is released under the MIT licence
reproduced below.


2. Prime World excerpts and the modifications we make to them
-------------------------------------------------------------

The patch steps in .github/workflows/ quote short passages of the Prime World
client sources verbatim in order to find and replace them, and they contain the
replacements we make. Those passages and those modifications are not ours to
relicense. They are governed by the LICENSING AGREEMENT (OFFER) of NIVAL
INTERNATIONAL LTD, effective 5 May 2024, published together with the game
sources, under which:

  - use is permitted for non-commercial purposes only;
  - modifications made by a licensee automatically become part of the subject
    matter of that agreement and are distributed freely, at no cost, and without
    additional commercial restrictions;
  - use ceases within three calendar days of a revocation notice published by
    the licensor.

The Prime World sources themselves are not redistributed here. The build fetches
them at build time from the community repository
Prime-World-Classic/prime-world-classic, whose own changes are, by the same
section 4, under the same agreement.

